# Copy to mobile/client/.env — gitignored, never committed.

# Same value the website's VITE_API_URL points at, but ABSOLUTE: the app has
# no dev-server proxy to resolve a relative path against. Use the versioned
# prefix (/api/v1), not the website's /api — see next.config.ts's rewrite.
#   Local:  http://192.168.1.X:3000/api/v1  (your machine's LAN IP, not
#           localhost — Expo Go runs on the PHONE, which can't reach your
#           computer's loopback address)
#   Prod:   https://alassema.com/api/v1
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=""

# Origin that serves root-relative media ("/img/seed-15.jpg" — the seeded
# catalogue and any legacy record). Leave BLANK in production: the deploy is
# single-origin (deploy/Caddyfile), so lib/assetUrl.ts derives it correctly by
# stripping "/api/v1" off EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL above.
#
# Local dev is the exception — there the API (:3000) and the images (Vite's
# app/public, :5173) are on DIFFERENT ports, so the derived origin is wrong and
# every seeded logo/cover renders blank. Point this at the running website dev
# server, EXPOSED ON THE LAN (`npm run dev:app` alone binds to localhost
# only, unreachable from a phone/emulator) — `npm run dev:app:lan` from the
# repo root to see them:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_ASSET_URL="http://192.168.1.X:5173"
EXPO_PUBLIC_ASSET_URL=""

# Google Sign-In — see lib/googleAuth.ts's setup note for how to obtain these.
# All three are PUBLIC identifiers (they ship in the app binary) — none of
# them is a secret, and none of the three iOS/Android/Web client types Google
# issues carries one.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=""
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=""

# Sign in with Apple needs NO key here, on purpose. The button appears whenever
# the running device supports it (a native check — see lib/appleAuth.ts), and
# the identity it produces is verified against the SERVER side's
# APPLE_CLIENT_IDS (api/.env.example). Two consequences worth knowing:
#   • It cannot be tested in Expo Go. The entitlement only exists inside a build
#     of this app, so use a development build.
#   • If the server has APPLE_CLIENT_IDS unset, the button still shows and the
#     tap fails with "Apple sign-in is not available." Set it on the server
#     BEFORE shipping an iOS build.

# Cloudflare Turnstile CAPTCHA — same value as the website's
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY (both point at the same Turnstile site). A PUBLIC
# identifier, not a secret — safe to ship in the app binary, same trust level
# as the Google client ids above. Leave blank to leave the widget off (see
# lib/captcha.ts) — matches the backend's own no-op-until-configured
# behavior (api's captcha.ts), so leads/feedback/reviews/waitlist submits
# keep working exactly as before either way.
EXPO_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=""

# Optional shared gate matching the website's VITE_API_KEY / the backend's
# API_KEY (api/.env.example). Unset on the server today, so this does
# nothing either way — but if API_KEY is ever set there, every request from
# this app needs the matching X-Api-Key header or it 401s (see api's
# proxy.ts). Leave blank unless the server side is also configured.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_KEY=""
